# irssi — real-world examples

## Connect to an IRC server

```
/connect irc.libera.chat
```

## Join a channel

```
/join #opensuse
```

## Set a nickname

```
/nick david
```

## Send a private message to a user

```
/msg <nickname> hello there
```

## Close the current channel window

```
/wc
```

## Switch between channel windows

```
ALT+<number>   e.g. ALT+1, ALT+2
```

## List the nicknames within a channel

```
/names
```

## Change the topic

```
/topic <description>
```

## Quit irssi

```
/exit
```

## Homelab: run irssi persistently in tmux on homelab

```sh
ssh david@homelab
tmux new -s irc irssi     # detach with Ctrl+b d, resume with: tmux attach -t irc
```

## Homelab: install on Tumbleweed

```sh
sudo zypper install irssi
```

| Command  | What it does              |
| -------- | ------------------------- |
| /connect | connect to a server       |
| /join    | join a channel            |
| /nick    | set nickname              |
| /msg     | private message           |
| /names   | list users in channel     |
| /wc      | close current window      |
| /exit    | quit irssi                |
